# Keep the working tree LF on every platform.
#
# Windows checkouts default to CRLF (`core.autocrlf=true`), and gofmt rejects
# CRLF: `gofmt -l .` then lists every .go file in the repo even though nothing
# is misformatted. The repository is already stored as LF in the index, so
# pinning the working tree to LF costs nothing and makes the formatting gate
# mean the same thing everywhere.
#
# `text=auto` still detects binaries (icons, wails metadata) and leaves them
# alone; eol=lf applies only to files git already considers text.
* text=auto eol=lf